Count II is withdrawn, respondent's counsel has acknowledged the withdrawal=
, and the remaining counts are moving toward settlement. Before this closes=
 I want three things written down, because I expect us to be asked about th=
is internally.<br />
<br />
The search that cleared Ottoway Trask is the identical search, in the ident=
ical archive, with the identical tooling and run by the identical two peopl=
e, as the search that made a custody case for this office last month. The s=
cope method was the same, the date envelope was constructed the same way, t=
he term lists were built the same way. The two searches produced opposite r=
esults, and the reason they produced opposite results is that in one matter=
 the documents existed and in the other they did not. That is the only diff=
erence, and it is the whole point.<br />
<br />
A null result from the journal archive is a finding and must be recorded as=
 one. Han-Wei's scope memorandum, both results indexes and Delphine's docum=
ent-by-document review go into the matter file as substantive work product,=
 not as administrative correspondence. If someone reopens this in five year=
s I want them to find the negative search rather than an absence.<br />
<br />
And the discipline that failed here is upstream of records. We pleaded the =
contents of a document nobody had read, on the strength of a free-text cell=
 in a spreadsheet, in a matter where we had a ready-made explanation for wh=
y the document could not be produced. That explanation was true in general =
and false in this case, and its being true in general is exactly what made =
it dangerous. A migration gap explains why a document might be missing. It =
is not evidence that the document was ever there.<br />
<br />
Camille Ostrowski